{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/741805-lunar-2e-to-3e-conversion","id":741805,"title":"Lunar 2e to 3e Conversion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-30T08:15:29-07:00","id":741805,"title":"Lunar 2e to 3e Conversion","content":"I was looking at <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/736824-ex3-lunar-crafting-charm-concepts\">this topic</a> and thought I should probably share my notes.<br /> <br /> This conversion assumes the user has access to 2e Lunars, 3e Core and the Scroll of Errata. It is written in Errata style, where only the changes are highlighted. Whenever a Charm has a significant wordcount, just assume it has the words &quot;Replace the Charm text with the following&quot;. It also includes a few Charms of my own creation to attempt to match the sheer size of the Solar Charm trees, even just the lower Essence effects. Also, apologies if anybody else's homebrew made their way here through my headcannon - I would cite you if I remembered where it came from. If you see something sufficiently similar, I'd be happy to credit you.<br /> <br /> The content is in the next few posts so that I can edit them as I keep working. I know I have a ton of keywords to put in, for example, and I haven't gone through the Scroll of Errata or even Strength/Dexterity/Stamina Charms.<br /> <br /> Again, this is some homebrew for a 'play right now' purpose not a 'dev's please do this' plea. It is a crafting project, not an instill action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T08:18:28-07:00","id":741835,"title":"","content":"Changing Moon<br /> <br /> Charisma:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Animal and Training Charms:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Dog-Tongue\" target=\"_blank\">Dog-Tongue</a> Method - unchanged<br /> <br /> Sharing the Gifts of Luna - Essence 1, Charisma 3 - The target's Essence rating is unchanged. Otherwise, same Charm<br /> <br /> Wolf Pack Training Technique - Essence 1, Charisma 4 - pre-req: Sharing the Gifts of Luna - Instead of the Mandate of Heaven part, this allows the Lunar to have Essence non-Charm successes on issuing an order to that group. The Lunar adds an additional success if that group contains a commander sharing the gifts of Luna from a commitment the Lunar controls. This may be used on Animals with the effects of Pack Instinct Affirmation if you do not currently have any familiars.<br /> <br /> Lesson of the Winter Wolf - Essence 2, Charisma 4, pre-req: Wolf Pack Training Technique - Instead of Conviction applications of Wolf Pack Training Technique it requires Size applications. Instead of Valor checks, this grants the unit perfect morale.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Holy Charms:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Outworld-Forsaking\" target=\"_blank\">Outworld-Forsaking</a> Stance - Ess 1, Charisma 3 - permanent - You do not need to use willpower to reject a change of an Intimacy initiated by Creatures of Darkness. The Lunar may still be inspired or reach a decision point as a result of a creature of darkness' meddling. The Lunar gains the benefit of a spent willpower when attacking or defending against Creatures of Darkness in physical combat that threatens one of the Lunar's Intimacies.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Foe-Turning\" target=\"_blank\">Foe-Turning</a> Rebuke - Ess 1, Charisma 4, Simple, Instant, Psyche, pre-req Outworld - Roll Charisma+(Social Ability) against one or several creature of darkness' Resolve with penalties for multiple targets as normal. Success means a rebuked creature of darkness must spend either 3 Willpower or her next [Lunar's Essence] actions must be either Disengage or Withdraw actions. In social combat, success typically means that creature of darkness leaves the scene immediately.<br /> <br /> Scathing Lunar Condemnation - Ess 2, Charisma 4, Psyche - Charisma+(Social Ability) may be used for both single and multiple targets.<br /> <br /> Fascination Charms:<br /> <br /> All Ess 2+, ask me then if Charisma isn't your Supernal.<br /> <br /> Interaction Charms<br /> <br /> Rapid Speech Technique - Ess 1, Charisma 2, 5m, Simple, Psyche - The friendly Lunar approaches her target for a Read Intentions action and asks so many questions so fast the target has a hard time keeping her composure. The Lunar may make two separate Read Intentions actions with this Charm with Charisma+(Social Ability), the first one against Guile as normal but the second one against Guile-1 as if an onslaught penalty. If either of these Read Intentions actions fail then like a normal read intentions action failure read intentions actions (including those produced by this Charm) can't be retried for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> Secret Speech Method/Falling Leaf Distraction - Ess 2, Charisma 3 or Manip 3, Mute - Charisma+(Social Ability). Similar to the Solar Linguistics Charm Letter within a Letter Technique on 3e Core page 323.<br /> <br /> Instinct Memory Insertion - Ess 1, Charisma 2, Mute - Supplements an inspire action to remember the message. This auto-succeeds and grants Charisma bonus dice to recall permanently.<br /> <br /> Perfect Fear Scent - Ess 1, Charisma 3, Psyche - With this Charm even death-cultists can be made to fear the Lunar's punishment. Supplements either a read intentions, threaten or instill action regarding discovering the target's fears, compel action, strengthen or create a fear of the Lunar respectively. When using this charm a normally unpersuasive threat can be made to seem persuasive (Give me all your silver or I'll tickle you!). Alternatively this Charm always meets the condition for retrying these actions with normal criteria. In either case the Charm cannot be used against the same target again in the story.<br /> <br /> Seductive Lust Infliction (previously Terrifying Lust Infliction) - Ess 1, Charisma 3, Psyche - With this Charm the Lunar can sell snow to Icewalkers or learn the hidden loves of Dynasts. Supplements either a read intentions, bribe or instill action regarding discovering the target's desires/hopes/dreams, compel action, strengthen or create a desire for the Lunar's friendship/respect/love respectively. When using this charm a normally unpersuasive reward can be made to seem persuasive (I'll give you an apple to let me use your house for a month). Alternatively, this Charm always meets the condition for retrying these actions with normal criteria. In either case the Charm cannot be used against the same target again in the story.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Hard-Nosed\" target=\"_blank\">Hard-Nosed</a> Denial Style - Ess 1, Charisma 3, Mute, 5m - The Lunar is true to herself and will simply not be moved if she is willing to tap into her divine reserves. Whenever the Lunar would spend a Willpower to resist an influence roll she may instead spend 5m. Using this Charm in a decision point can allow you both pay motes instead of willpower and also re-use an intimacy that has already been used to justify a resisting the influence of a decision point. This Charm cannot be used more than once in the same scene.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Military Unit Charms:<br /> <br /> Maintaining the Pack - Ess 1, Charisma 3 - When a battle group under the Lunar's command would normally roll for rout due to lost Magnitude it instead keeps its last point of Magnitude and the Lunar's next rally for numbers action on that battlegroup gains +2 non-Charm successes. This Charm can be used once per scene per battlegroup. Maintaining the Pack refreshes for a specific battlegroup if that battlegroup has both already benefited from this Charm this scene and later loses a point of Size.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Social Group Charms:<br /> <br /> Herd Reinforcement Stance - Ess 1, Charisma 3 - If new Intimacy conflicts with an existing Defining Intimacy it automatically fails with no roll. It can also be used to instill a positive intimacy of duty towards a legitimate leader.<br /> <br /> Forsaking the Blood Posture - Ess 1, Charisma 3, no pre-req - Same changes as Herd Reinforcement Stance. This Charm is sometimes called Culling the Pride Leader when used to create a negative intimacy against a specific leader instead of the society at large.<br /> <br /> Territory Charms:<br /> <br /> Boundary Marking Meditation - Ess 1, Charisma 3 - In addition to the normal effects, the Lunar is considered the leader of any native people (which can interact with Herd Reinforcement Stance and Forsaking the Blood Posture).<br /> <br /> Ranging Wolf Marking - Ess 3<br /> <br /> Sidebar: Owning Land<br /> <br /> Boundary Marking Meditation only supernaturally enhances a Lunar's ability and timescale to claim territory and punish those who displease her within it. Any Lunar with a Major or higher Tie to a territory that is not challenged for its ownership can be written as the owner by a few years of patternspiders' weaving and little god's reporting. This process can be sped up to a few months by claiming the highest rated Demense or Manse in the area. In the Wyld ownership can be achieved instantly by owning the Arcane Redoubt of a the highest rated Freehold or a Waypoint or set of Waypoints. Keep in mind that while a Lunar may be mighty in the territory they own they can always be dragged bodily from it by a higher power, though few such powers stoop to tossing Lunars about in the dirt.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Man-Tongue\" target=\"_blank\">Man-Tongue</a> Method - Ess 1, Charisma 3, Perception 3 pre-req: <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Dog-Tongue\" target=\"_blank\">Dog-Tongue</a> Method, 5m, Scene - The Lunar can speak any language spoken by the humanoid forms in her shapes library at Charisma 3+. At Perception 3+ she can understand any language spoken by the humanoid forms in her shapes library.<br /> <br /> Only the Strong Atemi - Ess 1, Charisma 2, Reflexive, 5m Indefinite - During and after a bloody battle the surviving veterans can be infused with Luna's Essence to be more than they could ever hope to be before. When a battle group you control loses a Magnitude in battle it gains 1 Level of Drill. At Essence 2+ this Charm allows Elite units to gain perfect morale. At Essence 3+ Elite, perfect morale units can gain +1 Might, and +2 might at Essence 4+. This Charm may be stacked up to the Lunar's Essence on the same unit, So a Size 4 Average Drill unit with normal morale could be changed to a Size 1 Elite Drill perfect morale +1 Might battlegroup after three applications of this Charm by an Essence 3 Lunar (thus committing 15 motes) over the course of one battle or several battles. Restoring the lost Size through later recruitment or dropping the mote commitment loses all effects of this Charm as the veterans are either diluted with green conscripts or lose the spark the Lunar has invested in them.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Manipulation:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Belief Charms:<br /> <br /> False Burrow Pursuit - Essence 1, Manipulation 2, Psyche, Mute - This Charm could cause a soldier on guard duty to check out the important disturbance or an investigator to chase either a dead end or the perfect lead as the Lunar desires.<br /> <br /> Mirror Sight Dismay - Essence 1, Manipulation 3, Psyche - With this Charm even devout worshipers can lose their faith and lead a secular life. Supplements any Instill Principle action so long as the Lunar believes the principle to be false. When using this charm a normally unpersuasive argument or emotional appeal can be made to seem persuasive (A patrician might be convinced that money has no power in this world by watching a relatively poor Dynast slight a rich patrician he knows despite all the other evidence he's seen of money's power - his Major Intimacy for Money (Covetous) could degraded to Minor). Alternatively this Charm always meets the condition for retrying an instill action with normal criteria. In either case the Charm cannot be used against the same target again in the story. Defense and Dissembling Charms:<br /> <br /> Mask of White Jade - Ess 1, Manipulation 2, 5m, 1wp, Reflexive, Round, Mute - The Lunar automatically wins any roll against their Guile for the rest of the round.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Cat-Face\" target=\"_blank\">Cat-Face</a> Presentation - Ess 1, Manipulation 3, 6m or 6m 1wp, Supplemental, <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Withering-Only\" target=\"_blank\">Withering-Only</a>, Counterattack, Psyche - The physical or social attack supplemented by this Charm is unexpected as if benefiting from re-established surprise. Normal cost if surprise, add 1wp if ambush. This Charm can be used once per scene.<br /> <br /> Commanded to Fly - Ess 1, Manipulation 4 - When resisting social influence, the Lunar may counterattack herself to change that influence to unacceptable by targeting her own Resolve-1 +any normal modifiers such as Intimacies. This use of Intimacies to make the counterattack does not affect their availability for use via spending willpower and vice versa.<br /> <br /> Feint Charms:<br /> <br /> Butterfly Eyes Defense - Ess 1, Manipulation 2. 3m and 3i, Psyche, Mute - When you suffer Initiative Crash you may force your opponent to spend 1wp or they are denied both the Initiative Break bonus and the knowledge of your Initiative Crash via this Charm.<br /> <br /> Butterfly Eyes Fist - Ess 1, Manipulation 4 - pre-req: Butterfly Eyes Defense, Psyche - Double the initiative granted to your ally from a successful distract gambit you perform.<br /> <br /> Interaction Charms:<br /> <br /> Chattering Magpie Inflection - Ess 1, Manipulation 2 - 5m, Simple, Psyche - The Lunar bludgeons her target with so many commands so fast the target has a hard time denying her. The Lunar may make two separate Instill actions with this Charm with Manipulation+(Social Ability), the first one against Resolve as normal but the second one against Resolve-1 as if an onslaught penalty. If either of these Instill actions fail then like a normal Instill action failure further Instill actions (including those produced by this Charm) can't be retried for the rest of the scene without further, greater argument (though these two combined only count as one attempt for that purpose).<br /> <br /> Perfection of the Mockingbird - Ess 1, Manipulation 3, Mute - No other changes<br /> <br /> Military Unit Charms:<br /> <br /> School Becomes Shark Formation - Ess 1, Manipulation 3 - Instead of double Magnitude, increase Size by the Lunar's Essence. This can increase Size beyond 5.<br /> <br /> Creating the Wolf Attitude - Ess 1, Manip 3, Psyche - For social actions instilling fear or benefiting from an Intimacy of fear the Lunar does not take the penalty for multiple targets when supplemented by this Charm.<br /> <br /> Feeding the Bear Progression - Ess 1, Manip 3, Psyche - For social actions instilling craving/desire or benefiting from an Intimacy of craving/desire the Lunar does not take the penalty for multiple targets when supplemented by this Charm.<br /> <br /> Face of the Moon Concealment/School in the Reeds Technique/Rats in the Basement Style - Ess 1, Charisma 2 or Manip 2 or Wits 2, 6m, Mute - A Lunar may pass along the tricks of concealment they know with supernatural effectiveness, even the hopelessly obvious can be lead to a position where they can ambush their foes with the Lunar's help. This Charm enhances an order regarding stealth to a battle group, but may be given to any willing allies even if they do not normally comprise a battle group. The Lunar rolls [Charisma or Manipulation or Wits]+[Stealth or Survival or Socialize], with the Attribute she used to purchase this Charm used and whichever Ability is most appropriate for the type of concealment she is instructing the battle group to take, instead of War. Successes are added to the average dice pool of the battle group, as per normal orders. If used to plan an ambush stratagem the Lunar may use Charisma+(Survival or Stealth or Socialize) instead of the commander's Intelligence+War if the commander allows the Lunar to plan the stratagem.<br /> <br /> Dissonant Birdsong Order - Ess 2, Manip 3, Psyche, Simple, 5m, pre-req: School in the Reeds Technique (or its mirrors) - The Lunar hears or sees the command a rival commander is giving their battlegroup and disrupts it - some soldiers are psychically prevented from perceiving the order while others see a different order entirely. The Lunar takes this action on the same tick as a commander she wishes to interfere with and rolls Manipulation+War where the successes the Lunar earns are subtracted from those the rightful commander's order making it weaker. If no successes remain (the Lunar's successes are the same as her targets) then the order is ignored but the battlegroup may act as normal. If the Lunar gains more successes than the rightful commander, the battlegroup skips their next action as the soldiers attempt to sort out the miscommunication. The Lunar typically has to delay their action to activate this Charm.<br /> <br /> Anglerfish Distracts the School Technique - Ess 3, Manip 5, Psyche, Simple, 7m, 3i, pre-req: Dissonant Birdsong Order - The Lunar can build a mirage in the minds of her opponent's troops so convincing they perceive it as an order from their own commanders. With this Charm the Lunar may send a non-attack command rolling Manipulation+War to any battlegroup on the field regardless of the Lunar's ownership of that group. If the rightful commander gives a command order between this Charm and the battlegroup's action, the rightful commander's command acts like Dissonant Birdsong Order for the purposes of cancelling the Anglerfish Distracts the School Technique order but need not be issued on the same tick.<br /> <br /> Snake Bites Tail Strategy - Ess 6, Manip 6, Permanent, pre-req: Anglerfish Distracts the School Technique - Once per scene per battlegroup the Lunar may give an attack order via Anglerfish Distracts the School Technique. This resets if the battlegroup loses a point of size.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Betrayal of Self or Shapeshifter's Kin - Essence 1, Manipulation 3, Mute - A Lunar can see when another wants to make a change so badly it is an Intimacy. Using this Charm a Lunar perfectly tells if any sentient being in their sensory range has such an Intimacy and what it is. If a farmer has an intimacy to become a travelling singer, she learns of this. If a Solar desires to be the best swordsman in Creation, she learns of this.<br /> <br /> Trickster's Way - Ess 3, Manip or Dexterity or Intelligence 4, 1m, Reflexive, Instant - Lunars are Luna's children, as fickle as dice and unpredictable as the wind. Lunars who have learned this Charm have internalized Luna's ways and can mislead thier opponents minds, words and arms simultaneously. Raise your Evasion, Parry, Resolve and Guile by 1 per 1m spent on this Charm. The dice limit for this Charm is equal to the highest limit of the four derived stats and interacts with stunted secondary attributes normally with the exception that Manipulation is always valid for the stunt even if it was already used to calculate the value (use twice Manipulation for Charm limits in that case).<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">(be sure to check out the Charisma Charms that have Manipulation mirrors)</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Appearance:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Hide of the Cunning Hunter - 3m, Reflexive, Indefinite, Mute, Stackable - The Lunar can gain the effect of the subtlety merit for any one feature they are currently expressing be it temporary or permanent. While most of the time this makes them look more human, it can also be used as, say, a bear to make them appear more ursine if they have a mutation that is not bear-like. This Charm may be activated once per feature and can explicitly be used on the Lunar's tell and Moonsilver tattoos in addition to supernatural merits, mutations or elements of shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> Perfect Symmetry - Ess 1, Appearance 4, permanent, Psyche - Dice gained from comparing Apperance to Resolve are instead counted as successes. At Essence 3+, the first [Lunar's Essence] successes are counted as non-Charm successes even if she used Charms to increase her Appearance.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">One of the Herd - Ess 1, Appearance 2, Instant - In crowds or armies can be used to re-establish surprise, enhance a Disengage or Withdrawal action. Reroll 1s on these rolls until they no longer appear.<br /> <br /> Recognizable Scars Removal Technique - Ess 1, Appearance 2, pre-req: One of the Herd, Duration: Indefinite, Cost 10m 1wp - Battle scars make for great stories but aren't convenient for the Lunar that might be an Immaculate postulate, a Guild spice trader and a Realm legionnaire in the same day all talking to the same<a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Dragon-Blooded\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon-Blooded</a> satrap. While this Charm is active, the Lunar quadruples her natural healing rate and can heal even unhealable injuries such as missing appendages or organs as if each were a number of bashing Incapacitated health levels equivalent to the Crippling scores on 3e Core page 201.<br /> <br /> Blood and Sinew Savant - Ess 3, Appearance 2, pre-req: Recognizable Scars Removal Technique, Permanent - Enhance Recognizable Scars Removal Technique to heal 5X instead of 4X as fast and unhealable injuries are healed as if -2 health levels. At this level of healing some Lunars become less than careful about courting injury. <br /> <br /> Ess 5, Appearance 2, pre-req: Blood and Sinew Savant, Permanent - Even the most savage beatings won't keep this Lunar from looking well for a society function the next day. Double all healing times (where doubling a doubling is a tripling - Exalted multiplication). All health levels are healed as quickly as -0 health levels. When using Recognizable Scars Removal Technique this also affects crippling injuries converted health levels.<br /> <br /> New Friend Aroma - Ess 1, Psyche - Can be permanent per 3e Intimacy rules, can be used once per story on anyone without an Intimacy towards the Lunar already.<br /> <br /> Observed Predator Instinct - Ess 1, Reflexive, Counterattack - When a challenge is made to the Lunar's Guile they may counterattack with a read intentions action from the source of the Guile challenge ignoring any retry restrictions on read intentions actions.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Glance-Oration\" target=\"_blank\">Glance-Oration</a> Technique - Ess 1, Permanent - Ignore the resolve penalty for using Gestures and Body Language (3e p221) and gestures can be used for any social actions not just seduction or intimidation. This can explicitly work through Secret Speech Method/Falling Leaf Distraction and other such Charms of different Attributes.<br /> <br /> Irresitable Silver Spiirt - Ess 1, Duration <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Scene-Long\" target=\"_blank\">Scene-Long</a> - MDV -&gt; Resolve/Guile. <br /> <br /> Military Charms:<br /> <br /> Diving Hawk Inspiration - Ess 1, App 2, 3m - Like the hawk diving before a thunderstorm, the Lunar can catalyze her troops to action. When using this Charm to supplement an action the Lunar can give an order to a battlegroup reflexively to do the same action on its next activation.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Tadpole or Claw Strider Simulacrum<br /> Cost: 15m, 1wp, Xahlvl, X/2 sxp, X/3 gxp, X/4 wxp round down<br /> Mins: Ess 3, Appearance 2<br /> Type: Simple <br /> Keywords: Salient<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Prerequisites: One of the Herd<br /> The Lunar makes an exact copy of herself and her mundane equipment, which briefly stands next to her true self, then her true self retreats to elsewhere as if yanked by the scruff. The Lunar sees through and commands the will-less copy as easily as any appendage. The copy has access to the same Charms and Knacks, with the same Attributes, Abilities, Virtues, Intimacies, Willpower, and equipment but the copy's mote pool is restricted to 5 personal motes and 10 peripheral motes, available immediately. The copy can only attune to artifacts this mote pool can sustain, though artifacts carried by the copy but attuned to the Lunar stay attuned to the Lunar and may be treated as mundane equivalents without the unattuned penalty. The copy can respire Essence and Willpower normally and heals at the same rate the Lunar does. The copy has as many health levels as the Lunar expended when activating the Charm, at those wound penalty levels (this means the copy may have indefinite wound penalties if no -0 health levels were used). Additionally, only craftsmen can infuse the copy with enough Essence to contain more than a single health level. Typically only one health level is used. That many are possible is a closely held secret of the Silver Pact. Tamuz once cut himself intentionally under the watch of a Wyld Hunt so that they would overcommit to hunting his copy down. He successfully faked his own death by being torn in half while falling down a waterfall while providing cover for a retrieval pack in Chariscuro. When the Charm ends or the copy loses its last health level the Lunar's Essence Copy and the mundane equipment she was copied wearing dissipate in an obvious display of Lunar Essence leaving no corpse. The Lunar's true self reappears safely where the Charm was activated. While in Elsewhere the Lunar respires no Essence, but does gain Willpower and heals any health levels not committed to the Essence Copy Charm as if sleeping even if the Lunar cannot naturally sleep. </span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":1103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","user":"Tikor","date":".  More edits, homebrew, and Dreams Charms 11-06-2015, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T08:19:13-07:00","id":741837,"title":"","content":"No Moon<br /> <br /> Perception:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Essence Charms:<br /> <br /> Eye of the Cat - Ess 1 - Everything except the fury stuff.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Devil-Restraining\" target=\"_blank\">Devil-Restraining</a> Grip - Ess 2 - Keep in mind Unstoppable Force vs. Immovable Object. Cannot go farther than medium.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#God-Cutting\" target=\"_blank\">God-Cutting</a> Essence - Ess 1 - Against dematerialized spirits double withering raw, converts decisive to aggravated.<br /> <br /> Spirit Maiming Essence Attack - Dual - After rolling the dice of damage on a withering attack, add Essence post-soak damage. On a Decisive attack, spirits destroyed by this Charm are destroyed permanently.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#God-Body\" target=\"_blank\">God-Body</a> Dissection - <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Decisive-Only\" target=\"_blank\">Decisive-Only</a>, Ess 5, Perception 5 - The gods of the Terrestrial Bureaucracy and even <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Yu-Shan\" target=\"_blank\">Yu-Shan</a> often overstep their place in the Lunar's eyes but this does not always warrant destruction, merely a lesson. Against the Fair Folk or demons sometimes their greatest powers need swept away before they fall like assaulting the trusses of a bridge. This Charm can target any being who is defaultly dematerial such as Spirits, most demons and the Fair Folk. This Charm enables the Lunar to eliminate powers from these beings as a gambit of difficulty equal to the Essence minimum to learn the power. See Lords 74.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Instinctive Essence Prediction - Ess 1<br /> <br /> Sense Charms:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Sense-Borrowing\" target=\"_blank\">Sense-Borrowing</a> Method - Ess 1<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Mote-Disruption\" target=\"_blank\">Mote-Disruption</a> Discovery (Previouly Inevitable Spoor Discovery) - Ess 1<br /> <br /> Sinister Strike Defense - Ess 4, Perception 5. Permanent, Cost \u2013, Pre-requisite: Eye of the Cat - When struck by an ambush attack this Charm automatically activates for 0 motes. The damage of the attack cannot fill the Lunar's last health level. The Lunar cannot die without seeing the blow that kills her, but she might still be surprised as this Charm has no effect on surprise attacks. No less of a death can take the Lunar from Creation. The Lunar who has achieved such enhanced vigilance cannot sleep, be incapacitated or lose awareness in any way. Treat the Lunar's incapacitated health levels as -6 health levels should she still be alive with a filled Incapacitated health level. Other effects that incapacitate are instead applied as a -6 wound penalty. Willpower generation is difficult for these Lunars, as the main method of sleeping is no longer available. NPC Lunars who know this Charm are suggested to have half their maximum willpower available unless they also have a powerful Cult.<br /> At Essence 5, the damage from such attacks is deferred till the end of the scene, but when applied still cannot fill the Lunar's last health level.<br /> At Essence 6, the damage from such attacks is ignored. What the Lunar does not perceive can no longer hurt them.<br /> <br /> Some sense enhancers. Don't know how to not <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Silver-Solar\" target=\"_blank\">Silver-Solar</a> this yet.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Military Charms:<br /> <br /> Bird Falls from Flock Targeting - Ess 1, Perception 4, 3m - When targeting the leader of a battlegroup or battlegroups, the Lunar's action supplemented by this Charm ignores any hindrance that battlegroup mounts such as Defend Other, making terrain rough, posting a guard or simply being in the way. She smashes through pike lines or walks among the group mistaken as an ally or dances between every watchful eye unseen as suits her temperament and skills but the result is the same - for this action the commander cannot hide behind her forces, the Lunar is always granted audience or faced in a challenge.<br /> <br /> Wolf Eye Advantage - Ess 1, Perception 3, Permanent - When on the hunt every second not chasing or killing your prey is a second wasted. When the Lunar takes an Aim action, it counts as two Aim actions.<br /> <br /> Eagle Eye Advantage - Ess 2, Perception 4, Permanent, pre-req: Wolf Eye Advantage - The Lunar can take another moment to hone in on her prey like the Eagle. When already at a +3 bonus from Aim, the Lunar can take another Aim action to increase that to +6. With <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Wolf-Eye\" target=\"_blank\">Wolf-Eye</a> advantage, short aiming will typically meet this criteria in 1 turn but Medium or longer aiming still typically takes two consecutive applications of Wolf Eye Advantage.<br /> <br /> Wolf Ear Advantage - Ess 1, Perception 3, 3m - The hare's footsteps in the forest bring a wolf to attention despite any distractions. This Charm negates all penalties to a read intentions action. The Lunar may re-attempt read intentions once per scene per target after failure if the re-attempt is supplemented by this Charm.<br /> <br /> Motive Dissecting Eye - Ess 1, Perception 5, Permanent, pre-req Wolf Ear Advantage - Once per scene the Lunar gets a free full Perception Excellency for a read intentions action.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Leaf-Falling\" target=\"_blank\">Leaf-Falling</a> Scrutiny - Ess 1, Perception 3 - roll against the target's Guile for targets concealing skills. <br /> <br /> Fellow Hound Insight - Ess 1, Perception 4 - The Lunar may explicitly exclude known beings from the search, such as packmates. The detection always succeeds for yes/no on type. The roll only determines if the highest non-excluded being's Essence is of that type, failure reveals that the strongest uknown Essence is of a different type (and might spur the Lunar to search again using a different Supernatural type). The types can be as broad or as narrow as the Lunar desires such as 'undead' or 'demons of the hierarchy of She Who Lives in Her Name' or 'any god that reports to a Calendar God'.<br /> <br /> Wyld Charms:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Wyld-Sensing\" target=\"_blank\">Wyld-Sensing</a> Instincts - Ess 1, Perception 2 - Instead of Magnitude 1, the Lunar can lead a battlegroup of Size (Lunar's Essence) even if those beings are not normally considered a battlegroup.<br /> <br /> Resisting the Lure of Madness - Ess 1, Perception 2, no pre-req - Instead of Magnitude 1, the Lunar can protect a battlegroup of Size (Lunar's Essence) even if those beings are not normally considered a battlegroup.<br /> <br /> (also some crafting Charms, let me know if you want to get into Crafting)<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Moonsilver Flicker Sense - Ess 1, Perception 2 Supplemental, Instant, 3m - Any reroll of a failed Perception roll may be supplemented by this Charm and gains Double 9s. This generally doesn't work by the time a hidden foe launches an unexpected attack but would work to try to find hidden characters prior to that point. Storytellers are encouraged to have players roll perception frequently for little secrets - not every missed detail is important.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#All-Senses\" target=\"_blank\">All-Senses</a> Expansion - Permanent - For non-battletime scenes, increase the duration of the Perception Excellency to scene. When using the Perception Excellency in battle increase the Duration to tick instead of Instant. At Essence 2+ increase that to round. <br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Blood-Kin\" target=\"_blank\">Blood-Kin</a> Echo - Ess 1, Perception 2, 8m, Simple, Scene - When the Lunar enters an area one of her ties has been, she instantly knows it with this Charm. To a Lunar surrounded by loved ones the very land feels welcoming even when they are not there. To the Lunar oppressed the land itself is a choking reminder of their oppressor. It is as if her Tie's scent is on the air even should she lack a nose to sniff with. She may choose to leave her current-day senses and visit any of the [Lunar's Essence] last times her tie was at that location as if she were there, subject to investigation with all her senses. While this happens, her original body is incapacitated. Most Lunars find a quiet place to lie down, but with a successful Stamina+Athletics roll she may remain standing through the experience. Her soul is free to wander the scene as an ignored observer. While this can be used to track prey the Lunar cares about (both positive and negative ties will do) it is more often used to remember a distant or lost loved one for those Ties can weather centuries. Some Lunars make yearly pilgrimages to last place they said goodbye to a lost love or kin to pay respects at the mountain or lake or battlefield of their last parting. Some elder Lunars pilgrimage out to see lost Ties in the Wyld places so remote only the Lunar's remembrance reminds the land that it was once Creation and keeps it from sliding into complete chaos. <br /> <br /> Moonsilver Cycle Prana - Ess 1, Perception 3, pre-req: <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Blood-Kin\" target=\"_blank\">Blood-Kin</a> Echo, Permanent - In the dreams of the <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Blood-Kin\" target=\"_blank\">Blood-Kin</a> Echo the Lunar can now interact with the shades her soul sees if she chooses to materialize among them. They react like ghosts who have no memory of her last cycle of visits and are a bit one-note regarding the subject of the past scene being recalled by <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Blood-Kin\" target=\"_blank\">Blood-Kin</a> Echo. This can be useful to question those that can no longer be questioned, or even predict the tactics and behavior prey might use when the Lunar finally catches up to their quarry though they would react as mortals do for the Flows of Essence are beyond the Lunar's magic to simulate. The Lunar can also interact with the scenery and can complete any craft project that can fit the work in the sequence of scenes accessible to <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Blood-Kin\" target=\"_blank\">Blood-Kin</a> Echo with the available materials, though she cannot bring the result back to reality. For xp purposes, the Lunar may only complete basic objectives relevant to the Tie that allows <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Blood-Kin\" target=\"_blank\">Blood-Kin</a> Echo to work, not any other shades in her Echo. Through repeated exposure to the same shades the Lunar might develop Ties sufficient for another invocation of <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Blood-Kin\" target=\"_blank\">Blood-Kin</a> Echo to function. Some Lunars use this Charm to attempt to pay penance for a regretted action or failure to be there in a time of need by repeatedly attempting to fix their failure. Most of these efforts are fruitless, for forgiveness must begin from within.<br /> <br /> Lifetime of Memories Labyrinth - Ess 2, Perception 3, pre-req: <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Blood-Kin\" target=\"_blank\">Blood-Kin</a> Echo, Permanent - The Lunar may now access Essence*Perception*(Tie Intensity) scenes for each location. While this doesn't truly provide a lifetime of scenes for <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Blood-Kin\" target=\"_blank\">Blood-Kin</a> Echo with enough travelling and wishful thinking, some Lunars pretend it does. A less heartbroken Lunar can use this Charm to retroactively shadow prey that they've left to roam while other matters required the Lunar's presence elsewhere. This is also useful for Lunars without the wealth of materials to try long-term crafting projects regularly but would like to further their craftsmanship on larger projects.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Eagle-Fish\" target=\"_blank\">Eagle-Fish</a> Transition Prophecy - pre-req <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Blood-Kin\" target=\"_blank\">Blood-Kin</a> Echo, Ess 2, Perception 3 - Creation's Loom is sufficient to reveal the weave of the past. A touch of the Wyld is needed to peek into the future. (rest of <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Eagle-Fish\" target=\"_blank\">Eagle-Fish</a> Transition Prophecy per 2e Lunars)</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Intelligence:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Defense Charms:<br /> <br /> Righteous Lion Defense - As per the Solar Charm of the same name on 3e 307 except that it functions on Defining Ties instead of Defining Principles. <br /> <br /> Intimacy of Hunter and Prey - Ess 1<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#True-To-The-Pack\" target=\"_blank\">True-To-The-Pack</a> Dedication - Ess 1 - may empower Essence+4 ties of Major or higher level. No interaction with Fury.<br /> <br /> Counting the Elephants Wrinkles - No changes<br /> <br /> Terrestrial Circle Sorcery - As per Solar Charm on p361<br /> <br /> Celestial Circle Sorcery - As per Solar Charm on p362<br /> <br /> Fluid Essence Refinement - Int 3, Essence 3, pre-req: Terrestrial Circle Sorcery, Permanent - Even the magical workings of the Lunars are survivors, refusing to give up and twisting away from tampering or dissolution. Increase the Difficulty of distorting the Lunar's spells by 1 for Terrestrial Circle Sorcery and 3 for Celestial Circle Sorcery. Each time a sorcerer attempts to counter the Lunar's spell, the first success is lost. Increase the Ambition of removing any of the Lunar's spells by 1. See Lords 76<br /> <br /> Essence Sink - 5m, Ess 5, Int 5, pre-reqs: Fluid Essence Refinement, Celestial Circle Sorcery - Double all the Lunar's threshold successes on distortion actions supplemented by this Charm. The Lunar is always considered knowledgeable of the spell for countermagic purposes when supplementing countermagic actions with this Charm. Lunars who know this Charm can explicitly flurry Distortion and Countermagic together, and when flurried one activation of this Charm will benefit both actions, but the actions suffer the normal flurry penalties.<br /> <br /> Sill Pond Infliction - Ess 1 Intelligence 3, Essence Days, Psyche - Roll Intelligence+Presence against a difficulty of a single target's Essence (or the highest Essence of a group at the normal penalty for group targeting). If you are successful the target(s) gain narrative amnesia for (Lunar's Essence) days - they can still speak, take care of themselves and are competent professionally as they were before but they cannot answer questions like what the day of the week it is, what their name is or especially what that Anathema looked like or where she was headed. They don't find anything odd about this and go about life on autopilot, resuming normal memory, even of the events during and before their amnesia when the duration is up.<br /> <br /> Burgeoning Wyld Affliction - Ess 2<br /> <br /> Withdrawal of Assumptions - Ess 3<br /> <br /> (also some crafting Charms, let me know if you want to get into Crafting)<br /> <br /> Lessons in the Blood - Reflexive - Gain a single Merit from a shape you know when shapeshifting into a different shape you know including your true human form.<br /> <br /> Predator's Insight - Simple (Misc action) - Ignore the xp stuff. See Lords 75.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Stick Them With The Pointy End - Ess 1, Intelligence 2 - Too simple to fail, that's how Lunars with this Charm like to plan their stratagem. When planning a battle stratagem the Lunar consciously focuses on making her plan simple to understand and execute, rerolling 1's on the Strategic Maneuver roll (3e p211). While the Lunar might still be overcome by a superior commander, she will not stab herself in the foot.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Shadowlands Circle Necromancy - pre-req: do not know Celestial Circle Sorcery - Once known, the Lunar may never climb to the heights of Celestial Circle Sorcery. She has embraced the power of the underworld, if only the first step.<br /> <br /> Labyrinth Circle Necromancy - pre-req: do not know Terrestrial Circle Sorcery - Once known, the Lunar may never learn Terrestrial Circle Sorcery. Her Essence has changed to reject Creation's elements and embrace the Labrynth's ash and despair. Note to readers: This is 3e, let's break some rules! Lunars vying Solars in Necromancy but both still being short of Abyssals is a fun twist.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Wits:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Spider's Trap Door - Ess 1<br /> <br /> Thieving Magpie Prana - Ess 1<br /> <br /> Many Pockets Meditation - Ess 2<br /> <br /> Meerkat Alertness Practice - Ess 1, Wits 4 - Once per scene the Lunar enjoys 1 full Wits Excellency to a Join Battle roll.<br /> <br /> Hungry Eagle Method - Ess 1, Wits 4, <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Withering-Only\" target=\"_blank\">Withering-Only</a> - The Lunar counters the next Essence withering attacks against her until her next action. She may activate this Charm in response to an attack<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Silver-Swift\" target=\"_blank\">Silver-Swift</a> Retort - Ess 1 - some new mechanic, come back to this one<br /> <br /> Serpent's Tooth Reply - Ess 2 - When subject to an inspire attack enter a Clash with the attacker - whoever loses the clash is inspired to do the action.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Exultant Battle Attitude - 10m, 1wp, Simple, Instant - Ess 2, Wits 4 - Once per battle scene the Lunar may roll Join Battle and earn initiative for a battle they have already joined.<br /> <br /> Fool You Twice Technique - 10m, 1wp, 5i, Simple, Instant, no pre-reqs - Ess 1, Wits 3 - All of the Lunar's effects that are 'down' are refreshed. Usable once per story and cannot be reset by other means. Can be used in or out of combat, out of combat ignore the initiative cost.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Many-Armed\" target=\"_blank\">Many-Armed</a> Monkey Style - Ess 1, Wits 3, 2m, Instant - Reduce the flurry penalty for both actions in a flurry to -0.<br /> <br /> Blinking Eye of Chaos - Ess 2, Wits 4 - (No other changes)<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Mongoose Spring Tactic - Ess 2, Wits 3, pre-req: Meerkat Alertness Practice, Reflexive, 8m - Once per scene, when you enter Initiative Crash immediately exit Initiative Crash by resetting to base initiative (3) and roll Join Battle gaining successes as Initiative as normal.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Furious Unhappy Recourse - Ess 1, Wits 2, 6m 1wp, Counterattack - When the Lunar is under attack while under a Defense penalty she may immediately and reflexively Clash her attacker. She skips her next action, and can go into an 'action debt' Essence deep with this Charm. Similarly for Social influence actions under net penalties to Resolve or Guile.<br /> <br /> Furious Debt Canyon - Ess 1, Wits 2, Permanent, pre-req: Furious Unhappy Recourse - When the Lunar uses Furious Unhappy Recourse all her Defense penalties are reduced by her current 'action debt'. She also has no limit on the 'action debt' Furious Unhappy Recourse can incur.<br /> <br /> Furious Reactor Stance - Ess 2, Wits 2, Permanent, pre-req: Furious Debt Canyon - Remove the willpower cost of Furious Unhappy Recourse. Reduce the mote cost of Furious Unhappy Recourse by 1 and an additional 1 mote for each 'action debt'. If Furious Reactor Stance would activate when Furious Unhappy Recourse already costs 0 motes, gain 1 bashing or lethal health level.<br /> <br /> Enactement of Fury - Ess 3, Wits 3, 10m, Uniform, <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Scene-Long\" target=\"_blank\">Scene-Long</a>, pre-req: Furious Unhappy Recourse - Your counterattacks gain Essence automatic successes. This applies to all counterattacks, not just Furious Unhappy Recourse<br /> <br /> Fury of Mind and Body - Ess 4, Wits 5, 5m, Uniform, Relfexive, Psyche, Furious Unhappy Recourse - Lunars are at their best at the moment of truth, and Lunars with this Charm make mortal adrenaline addicts' reckless behavior look like a casual night out. Clash attacks that you participate in grant you Essence initiative whether you win or lose. Decision points you enter or instigate grant you knowledge of an unknown Intimacy with your opponent. If she knows all the targets' current Intimacies they gain or bolster an Intimacy of &quot;Seeking Adversity (positive)&quot; as if she had successfully instilled that Intimacy.<br /> <br /> Furious Rebuilding of the Nest/Snakebite's Remorse - pre-req: Furious Unhappy Recourse - Ess 1, Wits 3, 5m, Simple - When a Lunar re-attempts a craft action from the materials scavenged from one of her previous craft actions she may roll twice during any resolve roll. This subtracts from the terminus as is if one roll and the time intervals are unchanged. Named for nesting Lunars' habit of re-building the perfect environment for their offspring several times over the course of gestation. This is also known as Snakebite's Remorse, for a Lunar may use this Charm to rapidly heal a would to a living thing that she herself inflicted. Use Wits+Medicine with 1 bashing health level restored per success or 1 lethal health level per 2 successes. Snakebite's Remorse may be reused so long as the original wound is still unhealed but no other health levels may be restored by this Charm. While her target's body may be mended, their intimacies towards the Lunar are rarely unchanged.<br /> <br /> Thousand Splinters Mending - pre-req: Furious Rebuilding of the Nest - Ess 2, Wits 3, permanent - This Charm upgrades Furious Rebuilding of the Nest. Now the Lunar rerolls 1's and 2's on a craft repair action when used. Also, she may heal the wounds of any living creature she personally senses while the wound is inflicted, though wounds she did not inflict herself cost 1wp per application of Snakebite's Remorse.<br /> <br /> Moonsilver Ripples Smoothened Technique - pre-req: Thousand Splinters Mending, Ess 3, Wits 3, 15m - Double all silver, gold and white xp gained when using the pre-requisites to this Charm if Moonsilver Ripples Smoothened Technique is committed for the entire project. Moonsilver Ripples Smoothened Technique also makes Medicine rolls to Treat Disease, Treat Poison or Treat Wounds including uses of its pre-requisites Basic Projects.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":1103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","user":"Tikor","date":".  More edits, homebrew, and Dreams Charms 11-06-2015, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T08:20:30-07:00","id":741843,"title":"","content":"Full Moon.<br /> <br /> Strength:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Attack Enhancement Charms</span></span></span> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Wind-Wings\" target=\"_blank\">Wind-Wings</a> Carry Technique - Ess 1, Strength 2 - Supplemental, Instant, 1m or 2m - For 1m you may attack with a ranged weapon as if you were 1 range band closer. This may change the aim requirements of your attack. For 2m you may attack with a melee weapon as if you were 1 ranged band closer.<br /> <br /> Agitation of the Swarm Technique - Ess 1, Strength 2 - Supplemental, Instant, 3m - Double DV penalty from onslaught. This normally doubles the onslaught penalty from -1 to -2 but some weapons or effects may change the onslaught value before this doubling.<br /> <br /> Ferocious Biting Tooth - Ess 1, Strength 3 - Supplemental Instant Withering-only 4m - Reduce your target's Parry by your Strength. The target may choose to use their Dodge for Defense in light of this Charm, so it works best against mundanely heavily armored opponents.<br /> <br /> Lightning Stroke Attack - Ess 4, Strength or Dex 5 - Supplemental Instant Withering-only 7m - pre-reqs: Ferocious Biting Tooth or Octopus and Spider Barrage - Parry and Dodge inapplicable.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Crippling Charms<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Foe-Marking\" target=\"_blank\">Foe-Marking</a> Style - Ess 1, Strength 2, 2m, <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Withering-Only\" target=\"_blank\">Withering-Only</a>, Duration: Indefinate, Stackable - If you succeed on a difficulty 1 scar gambit, your scar your target. Scarred targets remember their place. When someone the Lunar has scarred attempts to interact when them they are at -1 penalty so long as this Essence is committed (die pools, Defense, Resolve, Guile - any mechanical interaction, even soak). Some young upstarts need several reminders of their place, this Charm may be stacked [Lunar's Essence] times. While the Lunar sustains the commitment this scar cannot be healed, but will heal normally once the commitment is dropped.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Prey-Hobbling\" target=\"_blank\">Prey-Hobbling</a> Bite - Ess 1, Strength 2, 3m, <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Withering-Only\" target=\"_blank\">Withering-Only</a>, turn, Supplemental, pre-req: <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Foe-Marking\" target=\"_blank\">Foe-Marking</a> Style - If you succeed on the attack, your opponent cannot take the reflexive move action, but can take move as a combat action.<br /> <br /> Inviting the Winter Wolf - Ess 1, Strength 3, 5m, <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Decisive-Only\" target=\"_blank\">Decisive-Only</a>, Instant, pre-req:<a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Prey-Hobbling\" target=\"_blank\">Prey-Hobbling</a> Bite - When a Lunar wants someone to stay down, they stay down. If the Lunar's decisive attack deals at least 1 health level of damage, the Lunar breaks something that was probably important. Against foes with Exalted healing the Lunar's target is considered prone for the next [Lunar's Strength] rounds or until the wound is healed, whichever is first. Against foes without such healing, they're typically prone for the rest of the scene if not the rest of their life.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Fury Charms<br /> <br /> Relentless Lunar Fury - Ess 4, Strengh 5, Scene, 12m, 1wp, Decisive only - Decisive attacks both deal health levels and steal initiative as if they were withering attacks. Apply successes both against the target's health from the decisive attack and against their soak/initiative as if withering. Take this Initiative from the target immediately like a withering attack, but grant the Lunar the stolen Initiative plus the standard for 1 success after resetting to base Initiative from a successful Decisive attack. The Lunar's withering Overwhelming value is [Lunar's Essence]. This Charm does not benefit failed Decisive attacks.<br /> <br /> Lunar's Piercing Fury - Ess 5, Strength 5, Permanent, pre-req: Relentless Lunar Fury - Targets do not apply their soak to withering damage granted by Decisive attacks from Relentless Lunar Fury.<br /> <br /> Relentless Lunar Horde - Ess 5 - When Relentless Lunar Fury steals initiative the Lunar resets the Rally for Numbers action of a battlegroup the Lunar commands. If that unit had perfect morale instead once per scene allow a Rally for Numbers action, but this cannot be reset by losing a Size as normal. See Lords 70.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Damage Enhancement Charms<br /> <br /> Claws of the Silver Moon - Ess 1, Strength 2, <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Withering-Only\" target=\"_blank\">Withering-Only</a>, Reflexive, Scene - As per a Light Mortal Melee Weapon with Tags: Lethal, Brawl, Grappling, Natural. The Lunar can enhance any or all her appendages with a single application of Claws of the Silver Moon. The claws count as unarmed for Martial Arts style compatibility.<br /> <br /> Luna's Many Paws - Ess 1, Strength 3, Reflexive, 3m, Instant, pre-req: Claws of the Silver Moon - For an instant the Lunar could have a narwhal's tooth, a squid's tentacles or a ram's horn instead of the appendages she chooses to engage her enemy with. Gain any 1 tag or the Dual Wielding bonus to either your Unarmed or Claws of the Silver Moon attacks enhanced with Luna's Many Paws. This is not stackable, the Lunar must choose, but may have a different application on each attack. Yes, it can be ranged via the Thrown tag.<br /> <br /> Sharpened <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Moon-Claws\" target=\"_blank\">Moon-Claws</a> - Ess 2, Strength 3, Permanent, pre-req: Claws of the Silver Moon - Claws of the Silver Moon are now as per a Light Artifact Melee Weapon.<br /> <br /> Unstoppable Rending Claws - Ess 4, Strength 3, Permanent, pre-req: Sharpened <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Moon-Claws\" target=\"_blank\">Moon-Claws</a> - The Overwhelming value of Claws of the Silver Moon is now (lower of [Lunar's Essence] and 4) and they gain +1 Defense. <br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Impressions of Strength - Ess 1, Strength 3, <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Withering-Only\" target=\"_blank\">Withering-Only</a>, 3m+ - Grant double 9's to a Withering attack's damage roll. 1 additional mote can be spent at the time of the attack supplement to increase the Overwhelming trait of your weapon by 1 up to [Lunar's Essence] times.<br /> <br /> Rocks to Pebbles Attitude - Ess 2, Strength 4, Permanent, +3m+, pre-req: Impressions of Strength - Younger Lunars can casually tear a man in half and an elder Lunar's capacity for punishment is such that a warrior will sacrifice any ground to avoid it. Impressions of strength gains the Stackable keyword. Each time 3 additional motes are paid, the Lunar can double another success dice until double 7's at which point they begin to reroll damage dice that aren't successes starting at 1. If no such rerolls are available, instead triple 10s. This can be stacked [Lunar's Essence] times including the first activation and counts against the overwhelming boosting limits of Impressions of Strength. An Essence 3 Lunar could pay 7 motes (two Impressions of Strength with 1 Overwhelming bonus) for double 8's and +1 to Overwhelming. An Essence 5 Lunar could pay 15 motes (five Impressions of Strength) for double 7's and reroll 1's and 2's. An Essence 10 Lunar could pay 30 motes (ten Impressions of Strength) for triple 10's, double 7's and rerolling values 1 through 6.<br /> <br /> Undeniable Might - Ess 3, Strength 5, pre-req: Rocks to Pebbles Attitude, Supplemental, <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Decisive-Only\" target=\"_blank\">Decisive-Only</a>, 3m+ - Grant double 10's to a Withering attack's damage roll. 1 additional mote can be spent at the time of the attack supplement to decrease the Hardness trait of your target by 1 up to [Lunar's Essence] times.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Shell-Crushing\" target=\"_blank\">Shell-Crushing</a> Atemi - Ess 4, Strength 5, pre-req: Undeniable Might, <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Decisive-Only\" target=\"_blank\">Decisive-Only</a>, Permanent - Undeniable Might now ignores Hardness and gains Double 9s on the Initiative damage roll. 1 additional mote can be spent at the time of the attack supplement to increase the Initiative dice pool by 1 up to [Lunar's Essence] times.<br /> <br /> Unstoppable Lunar Blow (formerly Unstoppable Lunar Wound) - Ess 2, Uniform - (no further changes)<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Feats of Strength Charms<br /> <br /> Tearing Claw Atemi - Ess 1 - Explicitly compatible with the Strength Excellency (no further changes).<br /> <br /> Yeddim's Back Method - Ess 2 - Doubles Strength for the purposes of feats attemptable as well.<br /> <br /> Iron Tyrant Impact - pre-req: Only Yeddim's Back Method - (Lords 69)<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Lightning Flash Might Methodology - no longer exists, breaking stuff is a misc action.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Grappling Charms<br /> <br /> Roused Bear Throw - Ess1, Dual - The Lunar can now forfeit <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#StrengthX2\" target=\"_blank\">StrengthX2</a> turns for a throw or slam. When withering, gain double 9's. Alternatively, you can give any Melee or Martial Arts weapon the Thrown tag if it is not currently being worn. Weapons that already have the Thrown tag or are Thrown weapons gain 1 range band to their maximum range when supplemented by this Charm. Outside of combat, this Charm can be used dramatically on objects the Lunar would like to exit the scene via tossing; it is assumed the Lunar throws objects far enough that the scene would end before they are retrieved.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Cunning Wrestler Push / Clever Cat Pounce - Strength 2 or Intelligence 2, Ess 1, Dual, no pre-requisite - The Lunar positions their foe into their feral grapple or cunning trap. For withering attacks, the Lunar gains twice the initiative of the rolled damage (instead of the normal rolled damage) so long as their next action is a Gambit against the same target (the target loses the normal amount of initiative). If the Lunar does not attempt a Gambit next action then subtract this bonus Initiative. This can pull the Lunar out of Initiative Crash and put her back into it; if so grant the target of her attack the Initiative Break bonus and reset the 3 turn timer on Initiative Crash reset. If used to supplement a Gambit, the Lunar doubles the Defense penalties of her target for the purpose of executing a Gambit taking every advantage of their mistake in footwork or their bleeding gashes. A Lunar can use this Charm on a decisive strike already benefiting from the withering effect of this Charm.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Throat Bearing Hold is no longer a Charm, it is a difficulty 3 Gambit that must be performed as a savage in a grapple.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Wasp-Binding\" target=\"_blank\">Wasp-Binding</a> Method - Ess 1, Strength 2, no pre-req, Duration: rest of grapple actions or dramatic time - The solid Lunar Essence takes all the remaining grapple actions as restrain actions, freeing the Lunar for other tasks. This is primarily used so that the Lunar can herself benefit from penalties victims of grapples endure on 3e Core page 200, but artistic or dramatic Lunars may use this to hold objects bound in dramatic time after pouncing on them - the duration on inanimate objects or trivial opponents is one scene or until the Lunar drops the Essence commitment.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Porcupine Needle Spray (Formerly Cunning Porcupine Defense) - Ess 1, Strength 2, no pre-req, Dual, cost 3m, 1a, Simple - The Lunar shapes her anima causing needles of silver light explode from the Lunar creating an unblockable undodgeable attack on everyone in short range. Deal [Lunar's Essence] or 3, whichever is higher, withering dice of damage with a [Lunar's Essence] overwhemling trait. The Lunar does not gain this initiative from damage. This attack instead inflicts lethal damage to enemies in Initiative Crash and trivial opponents. This can explicitly be used while taking the restrain action of a grapple.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Moonsilver Lance Explosion - Ess 2, Strength 3, pre-req: Porcupine Needle Spray, Permanent, +1a+ - This Charm enhances its prerequisite by making the needles as large as the Lunar's arms or greatly increasing their distance. By paying an additional 1a the Lunar can increase the dice to [Lunar's <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#EssenceX2\" target=\"_blank\">EssenceX2</a>] or 5, whichever is higher or increase the range to medium. By paying for both effects she can enjoy both benefits. <br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Essence Charms<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Might-Bolstering\" target=\"_blank\">Might-Bolstering</a> Blow - Strength 3, Ess 1, <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Decisive-Only\" target=\"_blank\">Decisive-Only</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Breath-Drinking\" target=\"_blank\">Breath-Drinking</a> Executioner Attack - Strength 3, Ess 1 - Reciting a prayer to the Honored Foe, the Lunar may capture their death-Essence. No fury stuff.<br /> <br /> Greedy Mosquito Bite - pre-req: <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Might-Bolstering\" target=\"_blank\">Might-Bolstering</a> Blow, Ess 3, Strength 5, Permanent - The Lunar may forego the motes gained by <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Might-Bolstering\" target=\"_blank\">Might-Bolstering</a> Blow and instead gain that much initiative after initiative reset. See Lords 70</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Dexterity:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Balance and Grace Charms</span></span></span> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> Perched Bird Method - Mechanically equivalent to Graceful Crane Stance on Solar 3e 261<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Cat-Falling\" target=\"_blank\">Cat-Falling</a> Attitude - Ess 1, pre-req: Perched Bird Method, Uniform - Divide by [Lunar's Essence+1]. Also reduces the damage the Lunar suffers from throws but not slams.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Defensive Charms<br /> <br /> Secure Cat Stepping/Golden Tiger Stance - Ess 1, Stackable, 1m per -1 penalty - Can apply to Defense penalties at the time they are incurred (such as Choppnig and Smashing attacks' penalties or onslaught penalties) with a duration of turn or to any penalties for an instant. Can apply to Dodge or Parry.<br /> <br /> Finding the Needle's Eye - Ess 1, Dex 2, 3m, Counterattack - A Lunar may take the risk of greater injury to prove a point to those who would attack her from affar. When the Lunar or her charge are the target of a ranged attack she may immediately and reflexively Clash her attacker's projectile while gaining successes equal to her Parry/2 round down. If the Lunar succeeds she swats the projectile from the sky, but deals no damage to her opponent. If successful her opponent does suffer the -2 penalty for losing a Clash attack as normal as she gapes at the Lunar's ability to nullify her attacks. If she fails, she suffers all the normal penalties to a Clash attack (3e Core p202)<br /> <br /> Needle Redirection Technique - Ess 2, Dex 4, Permanent - The Lunar snatches a projectile out of the air and flings it back at her attacker using it's own momentum. Finding the Needle's Eye is now treated like a normal clash attack capable of damaging her opponent.<br /> <br /> Wary Swallow Method - Ess 1, Dex 3, Permanent - The Lunar suffers half the normal penalties to unexpected attacks. Her movements become avian in their quickness and preciseness no matter what form she wears and functions as an additional tell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Wind-Dancing\" target=\"_blank\">Wind-Dancing</a> Method - Ess 1, Dex 1, no pre-req, Uniform, Counterattack, 5m - A flighty Lunar can use the momentum of her opponents attacks and her own evasions to escape close combat. When the Lunar applies their Defense value they may immediately and reflexively take a Disengage action with bonus successes equal to the damage they took (0 if they successfully defended).<br /> <br /> Flowing Body Evasion - pre-req: <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Wind-Dancing\" target=\"_blank\">Wind-Dancing</a> Method, 6m 1wp, Uniform, Dex 5, Ess 2, Instant - Knowing the secrets of shape allow a Lunar to momentarily have no shape at all for her opponents to damage. Once per scene the Lunar may dodge any attack without a contest even recurring uncountable damage. Using the Charm reverts the Lunar back to their true human form and ends any <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Scene-Long\" target=\"_blank\">Scene-Long</a> Charms or Knacks. This Charm may be reset by changing to a form different from her true human form three times.<br /> <br /> Friendly Unmaking - Uniform, Perilous, Dex 5, Ess 3, pre-req: Flowing Body Evasion, Permanent - Flowing Body Evasion can now be applied to willing charges subject to the Lunar's Defend Other actions. Friendly Unmaking grants a different reset timer for each character that benefits from Flowing Body Evasion, but beneficiaries of the Lunar's protection rarely meet the reset condition.<br /> <br /> Flowing Body Ascension - no chnanges, see Lords 69<br /> <br /> Becoming Water's Envy - The reset condition for Flowing Body Evasion may be waived when used against withering attacks, see Lords 69<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#World-Bending\" target=\"_blank\">World-Bending</a> Guardian Attentiveness - A value of 1 in Creation, 2 in Bordermarches, 3 in Middlemarches, 4 in the Deep Wyld and 5 in Pure Chaos (subject to Charm dice limits). See Lords 69-70<br /> <br /> Native Son's Grace - pre-req: <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#World-Bending\" target=\"_blank\">World-Bending</a> Guardian Attentiveness, Permanent, Dexterity 6, Essence 6 - The Lunar may choose the lower of her Tie strength for the land she occupies or the value in <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#World-Bending\" target=\"_blank\">World-Bending</a> Guardian Attentiveness. Further, Once per scene in which the Lunar is in a place they own the Lunar may forgo the benefit of <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#World-Bending\" target=\"_blank\">World-Bending</a> Guardian Attentiveness and instead have the attack redirected to the scenery. This power resets if <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#World-Bending\" target=\"_blank\">World-Bending</a> Guardian Attentiveness is reactivated. See Lords 71.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Movement Charms<br /> <br /> Ground Denying Defense - Turn, Ess 1 - The number of opposing combatants that can be in close range of the Lunar is reduced to 3. If the scene already reduces the number to 3 or lower this Charm reduces that number by 1 to a minimum of 1. When another combatant enters, one leaves close to short (usually the last, but the storyteller can decide).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Blood-Brother\" target=\"_blank\">Blood-Brother</a> Battle Tactics - Permanent, Ess 2, Dex 3, pre-req: Ground Denying Defense - When the Lunar joins battle they may select one non-trivial ally to count as 1 opponent for the purposes of Ground Denying Defense. This designation may be changed as a misc action. When taking a defend other action with the designated ally as her charge, the Lunar can deny her opponent the ability to target her charge after succeeding her Defense with an attack.<br /> <br /> Furious Hound Pursuit / Retreating Fox Sprint - Ess 1 - Rush actions can now cover 2 range bands when the opponent moves away. Disengage actions now reflexively cover 2 range bands when successful and an opponent moves toward her.<br /> <br /> Moonlight Hunt - Duration: Instant - For that enhanced movement, not the whole scene, see Lords 70.<br /> <br /> Star Falls Through - see Lords 70<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Speed and Multiple Attack Charms<br /> <br /> Wasp Sting Blur - Ess 1, Dex 3 or Wits 3, 2m, Dual - This Charm enhances the initiative gain from a successful withering attack by 1 (usually from 1 to 2). It also reduces the initiative penalty for a failed decisive attack by 1 to a minimum of 0.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Twin-Fang\" target=\"_blank\">Twin-Fang</a> Technique - Ess 1, Dual, Perilous - Roll your attack once but apply it two times to the same target. The player may choose two withering attacks or one withering followed by one decisive attack and can see the results of the first before choosing the type of the second. Apply onslaught normally. This Charm can explicitly be used to do two savage attacks in a grapple even if the Lunar only has one control turn left, but otherwise takes two turns of control to do so.<br /> <br /> Octopus and Spider Barrage - 5m, 1wp, 5i per additional pair of limbs, Permanent, Essence 4, Dexterity 5 - The Lunar can strike with all the legs of the spider or tentacles of an octopus at once. After the two attacks from <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Twin-Fang\" target=\"_blank\">Twin-Fang</a> Technique once per scene the Lunar can add another pair of attacks as if applying <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Twin-Fang\" target=\"_blank\">Twin-Fang</a>Technique so long as she has two limbs that weren't part of the first <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Twin-Fang\" target=\"_blank\">Twin-Fang</a> Technique (typically <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Twin-Fang\" target=\"_blank\">Twin-Fang</a> technique uses both the Lunar's arms) and capable of launching an attack on her opponent from her current range. If she chose a Decisive attack in the previous pair and it was successful, she resets to base initiative like normal and this Charm will crash her without some other effect like Relentless Lunar Fury. This means up to 4 attacks is most human forms, one application of<a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Twin-Fang\" target=\"_blank\">Twin-Fang</a> Technique and one activation of Octopus and Spider Barrage. In a spider form this enhancement could be activated 3 times for 8 total attacks paying the cost for each attack pair activation. If the Lunar has some sort of natural missile such as thrown quills it counts as a single pair of limbs for the purposes of this Charm. Continue to count up onslaught penalties normally. After such a barrage, even if the Lunar fails to land anything, her packmakes can usually make short work of her dazzled opponent. This Charm has no native reset condition.<br /> <br /> Unhesitant Scorpion Lash - (no Ess or keyword changes) - Each time you give an opponent an onslaught penalty gain +1 initiative. See Lords 70<br /> <br /> Camouflaged Flounder Ambush - Ess1, Dex 3, 5m, 1wp, Dual, no pre-reqs - The Lunar fades from sight and strikes just as quickly. This Charm may be used once per scene to flurry a re-establish surprise action with an attack action at the normal flurry penalty (breaking the 3e Core page 203 rule that re-establish surprise cannot be flurried). This Charm refreshes if the Lunar is able to re-establish surprise without the aid of this Charm.<br /> <br /> Mongoose Strike Method - Ess 2, Dex 4, Permanent, pre-req: Camouflaged Flounder Ambush - This Charm removes the flurry penalty from any flurry containing an attack.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Stamina:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Defend Tree:<br /> <br /> Fur and Claw Protection - Reflexive, 2m - A Lunar using this Charm may use either dodge or parry for defend other by pushing their ward out of the way of attacks. <br /> <br /> Cucoon and Web Cry - Reflexive, 1 mote per soak, Duration round - When a Lunar's parry or dodge is overcome while they are defending other, they may use this Charm to bolster the soak of the target - be it herself or her charge - for 1 mote per 1 soak.<br /> <br /> Mother Bear Growl - 5m, Scene - The Lunar lets out a growl that warns anyone in earshot not to harass her cubs. When an opponent attempts to harm her charge while taking a defend other action her attack resets and she gains 1 non-Charm success on her next attack if it targets the offending opponent.<br /> <br /> Flock Protection Stance - 5m, Instant, pre-reqs: Cucoon and Web Cry - The Lunar's protection can now encompass [Lunar's Essence] charges in a single defend other action.<br /> <br /> Impossible Interception Style - 7m, Scene, pre-reqs: Cucoon and Web Cry - The Lunar's defend other actions can affect and continue to protect charges within 1 additional range band.<br /> <br /> Mountain Covers Valley Imposition - Ess 4, Stamina 5, pre-reqs: Flock Protection Stance, Impossible Interception Style, 15m, Scene - The Lunar can use defend other actions targeting battlegroups of a Size equal to or less than her Essence. When protecting smaller groups including individuals she gains the benefits of Flock Protection Stance and Impossible Interception Style. <br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Moonsilver Blade Trap - <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Decisive-Only\" target=\"_blank\">Decisive-Only</a>, Counterattack, 8m, 1wp, Ess 1, Stam 3, Instant - In response to a decisive attack that deals at least 1 level of damage the Lunar may trap her opponents' weapon within her body. This is of limited use for projectiles, perhaps for safe keeping to examine them later. When the opponent is holding on to the other end, however, the Lunar may reflexively launch an attack on their opponent. This attack is unparryable - the opponent's weapon is trapped and she is too close to interpose another weapon. The Lunar enjoys non-Charm bonus successes equal to the health levels lost if she uses this attack in a disarm or grapple gambit, reflecting just how deeply the weapon is trapped inside the Lunar's body. Against opponents unfamiliar with Lunars who have not seen this Charm before, the Storyteller might apply the Defense penalty for a surprise attack. After the duration is up, the weapon is released.<br /> <br /> Moonsilver Blade Swallow - Permanent, pre-req: Moonsilver Blade Trap, Ess 2, Stam 3 - This Charm upgrades it's prerequisite to have a duration of turn. An opponent holding a trapped weapon may twist it, which counts as an unparryable, undodgeable attack against the Lunar that can be either withering or decisive. She may not remove the weapon from the Lunar's hide or escape the Lunar without relinquishing the weapon, however. The Lunar only gains the reflexive attack when she first traps the weapon.<br /> <br /> Moonsilver Blade Fixture - Permanent, pre-req: Moonsilver Blade Swallow, Ess 3, Stam 5 - Increase the duration of Moonsilver Blade Trap to scene. The Lunar and her foe either kill each other, reach an end to hostilities or the opponent abandons her weapon.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Consumption Charms: <br /> <br /> Fertile Breath Inversion - Ess 1<br /> <br /> Moonsilver Stomach Conversion - Ess 1<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Ox-Body\" target=\"_blank\">Ox-Body</a> Technique - Stam 1/2 - Four -4, Stam 3/4 - Two -2, Two -4, Stam 5+ - Four -2. No Dying Health Levels.<br /> <br /> Flayed Hydra Technique - Ess 2, Stam 2, Permanent, Pre-req: <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Ox-Body\" target=\"_blank\">Ox-Body</a> Technique - Gain additional Incapacitated health levels equal to your Stamina. You are only killed if your final Incapacitated health level is filled with lethal or aggravated damage. Speed the Lunar's natural healing by a factor of 2.<br /> <br /> Steadfast Yeddim Meditation - Ess 1 - Stamina penalties. No fury stuff.<br /> <br /> Unstoppable Juggernaut Incarnation - can activate when taking bashing or lethal (instead of just lethal in the original text). If Flayed Hydra Technique is known, this can be used for any such Incapacitated health level that would be filled. When released, fill a -4 health level for each Incap delayed or a -2 level if all the -4 are filled. Higher levels cannot be substituted, if no such health levels are available when released, fill Incap levels, though this is usually only done when the Lunar's commitment is forcibly broken or she has delayed more levels of damage than she has -4 and -2 health levels combined.<br /> <br /> Moonsilver Juggernaut's Absorption (formerly Moonsilver Absorption) - Stam 5 - Now include aggravated damage to Unstoppable Juggernaut Incarnation. The Lunar may take a misc action to subtract her Stamina health levels from the damage recorded by Unstoppable Juggernaut Incarnation (but not the motes committed). This effect resets when Unstoppable Juggernaut Incarnation is released. See Lords 70<br /> <br /> Luna's Fortitude - change cost to 9m and add the Perilous keyword. While active you no longer take flurry penalties.<br /> <br /> Immortal Defender of the Land (previously Immovable Defender of the Land) - pre-req: Luna's Fortitude or Unstoppable Juggernaut Incarnation - no further changes, see Lords 71.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Environment Charms<br /> <br /> Environmental Mastery Technique - Stam 5 - As per <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Element-Resisting\" target=\"_blank\">Element-Resisting</a> Prana in 3e Core page 412 except Stamina rather than Resistance.<br /> <br /> Elemental Hide Enhancement (previously External Hide Perfection) - pre-req: Environmental Mastery Technique, Permanent - Environmental Mastery Technique can now protect against elemental effects that are from friends or Antagonists such as <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Dragon-Blooded\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon-Blooded</a> Animas. When used in this manner Environmental Mastery Technique gains the Perilous and <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Withering-Only\" target=\"_blank\">Withering-Only</a> tags and its duration is changed to Instant (which can drop a current invocation of Environmental Mastery Technique, but costs no additional motes when used in that manner).<br /> <br /> Elemental Hide Perfection - pre-req: Elemental Hide Enhancement, Ess 5, Stam 5, Permanent - The Lunar may now pay 1wp, 1a to remove the <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Perilous-Only\" target=\"_blank\">Perilous-Only</a>keyword that Elemental Hide Enhancement grants Environmental Mastery Technique.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Mote Charms:<br /> <br /> Silver Lunar Restitution - Gain 1wp instead of gaining motes, once per day. No mote pool increase. Lunars who somehow lose the ability to sleep find that their increased waking hours are best spent in vigilant guard.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Healing Charms:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Bruise-Relief\" target=\"_blank\">Bruise-Relief</a> Method - Ess 1, Cost 5m and 5i per bhlvl - No gift stuff. Yes, I specifically didn't put the Perilous keyword, better bring an edge to kill a Lunar (or deal Bashing faster than she can activate this Charm since it is limited each activation). I also like the image of Lunars healing faster when they're on the ropes.<br /> <br /> Halting the Scarlet Flow - Ess 1, Cost 5m and 5i per lhlvl, Perilous, Simple - Converts 1 lhlvl to 1bhlvl per 5i spent up to [Lunar's Essence] times per invocation. Counts as misc action that can be flurried with an attack. Commentary: Perilous needed here, for sure. Also note not reflexive.<br /> <br /> Mending the Broken Soul (Formerly Purging the Tarnished Silver) - Ess 3, Stamina 5, Cost 5m and 5i, Perilous, Simple, Instant - Converts 1 ahlvl to 1lhlvl. To heal further, this Charm must be activated again on another action. See Lords 70-71.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Soak Enhancement Charms<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Hide-Toughening\" target=\"_blank\">Hide-Toughening</a> Essence - Ess 1 - counts as natural soak.<br /> <br /> Frenzied Bear Fortification - Ess 1, Dual - Reduce Initiative damage taken by 1 for withering attacks. Reduce health levels lost by 1 for decisive attacks, but is inapplicable against aggravated damage. No fury stuff.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Wound-Mastering\" target=\"_blank\">Wound-Mastering</a> Body Evolution - Ess 2, <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Withering-Only\" target=\"_blank\">Withering-Only</a>, +3m, Permanent - When activating Frenzied Bear Fortification against a withering attack, the Lunar may pay 3 additional motes to reduce Initiative damage taken by [Lunar's Essence+1]. This enhancement only works against attacks that have dealt the Lunar at least one health level of damage from a decisive attack that scene.<br /> <br /> Wound Absorbing Predator - Ess 4, Stam 5, pre-req: <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Wound-Mastering\" target=\"_blank\">Wound-Mastering</a> Body Evolution, Cost Xbhlvl, <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Decisive-Only\" target=\"_blank\">Decisive-Only</a> - As the wolf dodges the worst of the stag's horns, so does the Lunar's hide only suffer the flat of her opponents' blades as she tears out their necks. Once per scene she may pay an equal amount of bashing health levels to ignore a single attack's worth of lethal or aggravated damage though the source of this damage remains the same. This Charm resets if the Lunar suffers as much lethal or aggravating damage as she has cumulatively used this Charm to ignore this scene.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Armor-Forging\" target=\"_blank\">Armor-Forging</a> Technique - Ess 1 - No gift stuff. When combined with Moonsilver armor or <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Moon-Face\" target=\"_blank\">Moon-Face</a> Mail instead add 1 soak per mote committed<br /> <br /> Stone Rhino's Skin - Ess 1, Perilous, pre-req: <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Hide-Toughening\" target=\"_blank\">Hide-Toughening</a> Essence, <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Armor-Forging\" target=\"_blank\">Armor-Forging</a> Technique - Set Hardness to your natural soak.<br /> <br /> Invulnerable Moonsilver Carapace - <a href=\"http://wyuli.tiddlyspot.com/#Withering-Only\" target=\"_blank\">Withering-Only</a>, Duration: Turn, Perilous - Reduce any overwhelming trait of all attacks against you to 0 when this Charm is activated. No bonus soak. Extension works the same. Usable once per scene, no reset condition.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Substance Charms:<br /> <br /> Scorpion and Toad Absolution - Ess 1, Permanent - Lunars with this Charm are supernaturally resistant to disease, acid, other harmful chemicals and poison (ill effects) and what the Lunar has survived before will trouble her less the next time. Add 1 success to any roll involving the Lunar these ill effects. Each time the Lunar fully recovers from the effects of one of these ill effects, add 1 to the success against effect. This has no limit other than the availability of such ill effects and the Lunar's ability to survive them. Elder Lunars enjoy gifting poisons to their younger sisters partly to harden them against them in the future and partly to mirthfully watch their effects typically after taking some reassuring action to prove the safety of whatever they're offering such as ingesting some themselves. Storytellers are encouraged to allow their Lunar players 1 effect they are arbitrarily good at resisting per story from the effects they already have some resistance to from off-screen re-exposure, even (especially) if no poison or disease effects came up that story. If no such effects are partially immunized against then the Lunar may name an effect. Lunars may choose to waive these bonus successes when contacting disease or poison, and find it useful to do so sometimes while in disguise.<br /> <br /> Scorpion and Toad Assumption - Ess 1, Type: Simple (combat time), Cost 3m, 3i - Instead of 5 minutes, this Charm can be activated in combat time. <br /> <br /> Scorpion and Toad Mastery - Ess 2 - (no other changes)<br /> <br /> Adder Fang Method - Change all damages to initiative, change all intervals of tick to round, give a Duration of [Lunar's Essence+1] turns, ignore toxicity, a Resource value of 3, and the vector is envenomed weapon (which might be natural in the Lunar's case). No gift effect. This Charm is especially useful for poisoning fellow Lunars since so many of them are highly resistant to most naturally occurring poisons.<br /> <br /> Scorpion and Toad Liver - Ess 1, pre-req:Scorpion and Toad Absolution, 4m, Duration: Instant, Reflexive - Your natural soak and any hardness apply to the ill effects covered by Scorpion and Toad Assumption. If unspecified Poisons have an overwhelming trait of 1 and environmental hazards have an overwhelming trait of 0 though the ST may choose to increase these values for truly epic poisons or hazards. This Charm needs to be applied multiple times to resist ill effects on different turns, but works on all effects for the instant it is activated.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":1103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","user":"Tikor","date":".  More edits, homebrew and Dreams Charms 11-06-2015, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T08:21:43-07:00","id":741845,"title":"","content":"Knacks. I'm much more in the camp of 'a Lunar can change into anything' than the 'animals only' camp. Maybe the devs will make it cool enough to adjust my headcannon with the 3e release.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Second Soul Form - Ess 1, Intelligence 1, Permanent, No pre-reqs - A Lunar's Spirit Shape matches their nature at their moment of Exaltation but the Lunars are mecurial beings and half-human besides. They grow and change. This Charm allows the user, after sufficient introspection, to recognize how they have grown in character or temperment closer to another form known to them than their existing Spirit Shape(s). That form becomes a second Spirit Shape, and is considered a true form in all ways. The Lunar retains access to their first Spirit Shape, for though she has changed she can always remember who she once was. This Charm may be repurchased at Ess 2, Int 2; Ess 3, Int 3; etc. to cover a new form each time though excessive Spirit Shapes are marks of chimerism to many Silver Pact Lunars.<br /> <br /> Humble Mouse Shape - Ess 1, Wits 2<br /> Emerald Grasshopper Form - Prerequisites: Humble Mouse Shape, Essence 2, Wits 3<br /> Towering Beast Form: Ess 1, Stamina 2<br /> Mountainous Spirit Expression: Ess 2, Stamina 3<br /> Prey's Skin Disguise: Essence 1, does not require a WP to change shape just the normal cost.<br /> (I remember you didn't want to eat people, so the rest of the tree I didn't look at)<br /> <br /> Green Sun Child: Ess 3, All Demons and Yozi are valid targets respecting size limits<br /> Heart-Theft of the Behemoth: Ess 4, pre-req Towering Beast Form and Luna's Hidden Face, all behemoths, be they Wyld or otherwise, are valid if fit size description.<br /> World-Theft of Primordial: Ess 6, pre-req Heart-Theft of the Behemoth: Behemoths of any size as well as the world-bodies of the Primordials or the Death-tombs of the Neverborn are valid targets for the sacred hunt. Extend the time for the consumption part of the hunt to 6 days as the Lunar gorges herself on the truly massive being she wishes to emulate.<br /> Hearth and Flame: Ess 2<br /> Luna's Hidden Face: Ess 2, Perception 3. All Wyld denizes short of behemoth are valid targets for the Sacred Hunt (but some may also require Humble Mouse Shape or Towering Beast Form because size limits).<br /> <br /> Life of Hummingbird - Essence 1<br /> Lessons in the Blood - Lunars 2e p189, Essence 2 - pre-req Life of Hummingbird, refreshes once per story.<br /> Hybrid Body Rearrangement - Ess 1, Wits 3<br /> Changing Plumage Ess 1<br /> Internal Form Mastery - Ess 1 and all attributes besides Appearance<br /> Subtle Silver Declaration - Ess 1, Apperance 2. 1 mote, Reflexive Indefinate - replace text with: Your tell is impossible to percieve (roll-offs with Appearance+Survival). When changing forms this Charm must be reactivated or the effect is lost.<br /> Twin Faced Hero = Ess 1, Wits 2. Also allows hermaphrodite forms.<br /> <br /> Quicksilver Second Face - Ess 1, Dex 3, 3m - Shapeshifting in battle or mid-conversation can throw an opponent off-guard, especially when done quickly and unexpectedly. When the Lunar shapeshifts in battle they gain Essence initiative and can flurry another action without penalty. When the Lunar shapeshifts in social combat, they gain Essence non-Charm successes to their next social attack though without some way to communicate this has limited use such as escalating a prior intimidate attempt. Quicksilver Second Face cannot be used again until a significant opponent successfully defends one of the Lunar's physical or social attacks with Defense or Resolve or Guile - when the opponent thinks they have the new form understood the Lunar can change shape with similar off-settling results once more but even then a new form must be used that has not been seen by this opponent this scene.<br /> Lightning Change Style - Ess 1, Dex 4, Supplemental, 3m - Using this Charm makes one shapeshifting action Reflexive. It can stack with the bonuses from Quicksilver Second Face though the flurry benefit is no longer relevant.<br /> Constant Quicksilver Rearrangement - Ess 2, Wits 5, Supplemental, 5m, Duration: one turn - The Lunar can take any number of known forms without paying further shapeshifting mote costs for the remainder of her turn and all such shapeshifts are reflexive. See uses in Lunars 2e p136.<br /> <br /> DBT in 3e section - Ess 1, Strength 3<br /> Perfected Hybrid Interaction - Ess 1, Wits 2, Permanent - Double the bonus to any 1 DBT benefit. For example, one Lunar may purchase this Charm and enjoy +8 to withering attacks' raw damage through the strength of a yeddim, but still only benefit +4 to her movement pool and soak. For this Charm, the Lunar is not limited to the theme of their Spirit Shape or even their known forms, but may incorporate any animal's traits they know to enhance their combat prowess. This Charm is repurchasable at Ess 2, Wits 3 and Essence 3, Wits 4. Any repurchase must benefit a different bonus; no bonus may be raised beyond double.<br /> Terrifying Beastman Alteration - Ess 2, Appearance 3, Permanent - The Lunar may incorporate Essence*3 dots of Innate merits, even Supernatural merits, into their Deadly Beastman Form. This Charm may be repurchased at the stated minimums. When the Lunar raises their Essence or repurchases this Charm they may completely rearrange the dots of Innate merits.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T08:22:47-07:00","id":741846,"title":"","content":"Houserules:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Changing Moon Anima, all reflexive: a - go to Dim. 2a - free shapeshift and go to Dim. 3a - Free 1 band movement, +3 successses to re-establishing stealth, free shapeshift, go to dim.<br /> Knacks do not grant excellencies.<br /> Supernal Attributes grant Ess 5 for Charms and Knacks both.<br /> The Wyld keyword is still around but used for only the truly weird stuff like Eagle-Fish Prophecy.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Character Creation:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Step 1: As per 2e Lunar<br /> Step 2: As per 2e Lunar, but choose one Supernal Attribute from among Caste Attributes (Favored if Casteless).<br /> Step 3: As per 2e Lunar<br /> Step 4: As per 3e Solar<br /> Step 5: 12 Charms<br /> Step 6: As per 3e Solar<br /> Step 7: As per 3e Solar<br /> Step 8: As per 3e Solar except for Essence pools which are in 3e Core page 545<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Caste Ability choice lists:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Full Moon: Strength, Dexterity, Stamina, Wits</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Changing Moon: Charisma, Manipulation, Appearance, Dexterity</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">No Moon: Perception, Intelligence, Wits, Charisma</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> General Charms:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Excellencies:<br /> 1st is found in 3e Core p545.<br /> Flawless Natural Focus - Ess 1, Intelligence 3 - The Lunar understands their natural aptitude well enough to hone it in a specific direction, resulting in the ability to learn specialties for Attributes just as they would for Abilities. Purchase of this Charm grants 1 free Specialty dot that must be spent on an Attribute Specialty. See Lunars 2e p141-142 for appropriate Attribute specialty scopes.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":1103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","user":"Tikor","date":".  Added Caste Attribute lists 11-01-2015, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T10:02:44-07:00","id":742150,"title":"","content":"Here's my honest advice:<br /> <br /> Converting 2e Lunars charms to 3e like this is not going to work; the systems and their assumptions are just too different.<br /> <br /> If you want something quick and dirty and playable, then rather than starting with 2e Lunars as a base and trying to upgrade, I would suggest starting with 3e Solars as a base and trying to tweak it to reflect the parts of 2e Lunars you find important. Obviously this will produce a Silver Solars-ish Lunars, but it's the only option that I think is likely to produce something remotely balanced and playable in a reasonable timeframe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T14:19:57-07:00","id":742854,"title":"","content":"I agree the system used for many Lunar 2e Charms is incompatible - that is why I'm converting them. Many of the Charms share only a name and a broad concept with entirely new mechanical bits interacting with the new systems. Some interacted with the storyteller system only on an Attribute or Ability level and needed only their Essence minimum adjusted. Some Attributes have their trees rearranged, many flattened, some Charms were omitted, others added. Much like Call the Blade, Heavenly Guardian Defense and Solar Counterattack and the Solar Melee tree, but unlike your Silver-Solar suggestion they have a more Lunar flavor. I encourage you to read them. <br /> <br /> I concede these might not be balanced. I have no playtesters but my own table. I do not concede that it is not going to work/impossible. This is Exalted!<br /> \u200b<br /> I've updated with another 10 Strength Charm conversions including the always controversial Claws of the Silver Moon! Taking a break to read the Grapple rules another 3 times before trying to do that tree of Charms and Gambits in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":1103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","user":"Tikor","date":".  Spacing 10-30-2015, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T15:57:31-07:00","id":743135,"title":"","content":"I tried converting a few bits of 3e Lunars (before I realized that they'd be out after Exigents and stopped):<ul><li><b>Do not make knacks. Make the shapeshifting stuff all charm based</b>. The sole reason they had knacks was to prevent the Eclipse abuses, and now this is no longer a worry. It gives you more freedom and quite a few times, even in 2.Xe, I was going &quot;I want to make a charm, but it kinda does what a knack does but still not knack like enough to needs to be a charm, shit.&quot;</li> <li>When making charms remember that Lunars will have access to a warform and their animal form. This makes charm balancing a lot more complicated.</li> <li>Doubling onslaught should be 3m 2i or 5m.</li> <li>Unblockable and undodgable was a thing in 2.Xe, it was gutted massively for 3e.</li> </ul><br /> Good luck overall though. Making Lunars in 3e is a bit difficult as they have a rougher base. Even Sidereals would be easier to make in 3e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T18:16:49-07:00","id":743399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/741805-lunar-2e-to-3e-conversion?p=743135#post743135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>When making charms remember that Lunars will have access to a warform and their animal form. This makes charm balancing a lot more complicated.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>This one is particularly important (and it's easy to miss.) In 1e and 2e, persistent dice-adders were common, and shapeshifting was ultimately just another &quot;flavor&quot; of that, so it wasn't such a big deal.<br /> <br /> In 3e, persistent dice-adders for combat are practically nonexistent, so the impact of a warform or animal form is dramatically higher (especially since animals have higher stats overall in 3e.) Pretty much all of shapeshifting and the entire Lunar charmset is going to have to be built around this fact.<br /> <br /> OTOH you don't want to end up with a situation where Lunar charms suck because of DBT, and you want fighting in human form to be an option, so I suspect that what you'll see are several charms that are weaker in DBT / animal form, or which give you additional bonuses when you're in human form. We already know Lunars can't use evocations in DBT form, which is likely part of this; I wouldn't be surprised if MA has similar limitations (eg. no Celestial benefits in animal / DBT form.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T20:20:14-07:00","id":743610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/741805-lunar-2e-to-3e-conversion?p=743399#post743399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't be surprised if MA has similar limitations (eg. no Celestial benefits in animal / DBT form.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Last I heard, it's IMPOSSIBLE to use Martial Arts in animal forms. No Tiger Style for tigers!<br /> <br /> Tiger Style is designed for humans to use in emulation of a tiger. But a tiger (or, more to the point, a crane or a snake or any other form a Tiger Stylist Lunar might take) isn't built like a human, and cannot fight like a human pretending to be a tiger. A tiger's ability to fight like itself is already factored into its stats, natural weapons, and special features.<br /> <br /> By the same token, any Style that a sapient tiger might develop would be impossible for a human to perform, just as no human could perform the Dagger Wing Style of the Pterok Dragon Kings.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think that Silver-Voiced Nightingale Style gets a pass, though, since its original form is based in having a voice rather than using your limbs. Though if you are a Stylist who normally uses handheld instruments or language-based Sick Burn rapping, you'd better get back to basics.<br /> <br /> <br /> You'd better believe that after I learned of this restriction, I jokingly asked the developers what forms locked Lunars out of using sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T08:31:05-07:00","id":744518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/741805-lunar-2e-to-3e-conversion?p=743399#post743399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 3e, persistent dice-adders for combat are practically nonexistent, so the impact of a warform or animal form is dramatically higher (especially since animals have higher stats overall in 3e.) Pretty much all of shapeshifting and the entire Lunar charmset is going to have to be built around this fact.<br /> <br /> OTOH you don't want to end up with a situation where Lunar charms suck because of DBT, and you want fighting in human form to be an option, so I suspect that what you'll see are several charms that are weaker in DBT / animal form, or which give you additional bonuses when you're in human form. We already know Lunars can't use evocations in DBT form, which is likely part of this; I wouldn't be surprised if MA has similar limitations (eg. no Celestial benefits in animal / DBT form.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been staying away from the persistent dice adders. Removing shapes might be a neat restriction on Charms, I've worked that into my version of Flowing Body Evasion (will post soon).<br /> <br /> I refuse to believe grapple-bonus charms won't work just as well or even better if you are a literal gorilla. For every shape that would make a Charm enhancing action that would seem odd or perhaps be weaker (range bonuses to ranged attacks if you are a rhino?) there's going to be a grapple/gorilla example. This sounds like a hard problem, out of the scope of my homebrew. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T10:40:24-07:00","id":744696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/741805-lunar-2e-to-3e-conversion?p=744518#post744518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">my version of Flowing Body Evasion (will post soon).</div> </div> </div> </div>Posted! ...(10 characters)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T19:28:38-07:00","id":745569,"title":"","content":"I notice you've made some charms and knacks less restrictive. In 3e, shouldn't they be more restrictive, or weaker? Since the power level is reduced?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T20:34:28-07:00","id":745667,"title":"","content":"You really ought to uses spaces between lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T09:23:32-08:00","id":746786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/741805-lunar-2e-to-3e-conversion?p=744518#post744518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I refuse to believe grapple-bonus charms won't work just as well or even better if you are a literal gorilla. For every shape that would make a Charm enhancing action that would seem odd or perhaps be weaker (range bonuses to ranged attacks if you are a rhino?) there's going to be a grapple/gorilla example. This sounds like a hard problem, out of the scope of my homebrew.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that leaves you with only a few options:<br /> <br /> 1. Gorilla Lunars are literally unbeatable in a grapple, because they're throwing around ridiculously big dice pools for free, plus powerful Celestial-level charms. Remember, Lunars aren't going to be the only people who have &quot;grapple really well&quot; as a theme. Letting the Lunar gorilla grappler get his hands on you is probably a bad idea no matter who you are, but there have to be people at least competitive with them, and I don't see any way to do it if Lunars get massive gorilla strength <i>plus</i> grappling charms on par with everyone else who is good at it.<br /> <br /> 2. Lunar grappling charms are noticeably weaker compared to any other Celestial splat that has a grapple build, or their overall grappling suite, relative to everyone else's, has holes in them that you're supposed to use turning into a gorilla to fix. This means that it's impossible to be a really good Lunar grappler without turning into a gorilla; that's at least <i>plausible</i> design, but I don't think it's where things will go.<br /> <br /> 3. Lunars have grappling charms that have extra bonuses when you're in human form, or which are somehow incompatible with the bonuses from being a gorilla, or cost more when you're a gorilla or whatever.<br /> <br /> Making Lunar grapple-bonus charms work as well or better when you're an actual gorilla means you end up with Lunars that are either hilariously unbeatable in gorilla form, or noticeably worse grapplers than other grapple-focused Celestials in human form.<br /> <br /> I suspect that the best answer is something akin to 3, but to do it in a subtle way that doesn't immediately leap off the page as &quot;this charm is weaker when you're a gorilla&quot;. For instance, Lunars might have a &quot;strength of a gorilla&quot; that raises your strength to a gorilla's even when you're in human form -- this feels thematically appropriate, and the fact that it doesn't actually do anything when you're already a gorilla (or maybe has some alternate minor effect, to keep it from being useless) doesn't leap off the page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 11-01-2015, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T10:18:03-08:00","id":746994,"title":"","content":"I agree with Aquillion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T10:28:12-08:00","id":747011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/741805-lunar-2e-to-3e-conversion?p=746786#post746786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that leaves you with only a few options:<br /> <br /> 3. Lunars have grappling charms that have extra bonuses when you're in human form, or which are somehow incompatible with the bonuses from being a gorilla, or cost more when you're a gorilla or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making dice in excess of the character's normal dice from shape-shifting count as dice from Charms seems like a readily available anti-stacking restriction that would put the best Lunar grappler, when stunting, on par with other Celestials. <br /> <br /> Having lots of ways to effectively get scene-long dice is hard to balance, I do not disagree. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/741805-lunar-2e-to-3e-conversion?p=745569#post745569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I notice you've made some charms and knacks less restrictive. In 3e, shouldn't they be more restrictive, or weaker? Since the power level is reduced?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'd like to go with weaker, because I like broad applicability as a Lunar theme. Any particular ones you think are too powerful given their breadth? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T10:44:02-08:00","id":747030,"title":"","content":"Still not reading any of that without spaces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T11:20:14-08:00","id":747083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/741805-lunar-2e-to-3e-conversion?p=746786#post746786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ape stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>See, this is my one problem with Lunar design, in that some animal forms are basically god tier.<br /> <br /> &quot;I don't want to turn into a Gorilla&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Too bad, enough your weakened grapple charms because you COULD turn into a Gorilla.&quot;<br /> <br /> I like your idea of getting bonuses when in human form though, like how devs said you could 'grow out of' DBT or animal forms if you wanted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T12:46:24-08:00","id":747216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/741805-lunar-2e-to-3e-conversion?p=745667#post745667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You really ought to uses spaces between lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've added spacing to the Full Moon post. If you tell me that's more readable, I'll do the rest on the next edit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T14:31:48-08:00","id":747469,"title":"","content":"Yes, that's more readable. I can distinguish the individual paragraphs now, instead of seeing an innavigable wall of text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T17:29:41-08:00","id":747967,"title":"","content":"Spacing added to the rest of the Charms posts (also some light editing).<br /> <br /> I also put in lists for Caste Attribute choices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T19:47:35-08:00","id":748243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/741805-lunar-2e-to-3e-conversion?p=747011#post747011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making dice in excess of the character's normal dice from shape-shifting count as dice from Charms seems like a readily available anti-stacking restriction that would put the best Lunar grappler, when stunting, on par with other Celestials.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a start, but it alone is not enough in 3e. Remember that in 3e, IAM (and its equivalents) do not exist. For most people, scenelong dice-adders are simply not a thing; getting five extra scenelong dice, <i>even if they're not cap-busting</i>, is basically like getting five extra motes an action, and absent other concerns it means that over the course of a fight you're going to trivially crush almost everyone, since they're going to have to burn motes every action just to keep up with you.<br /> <br /> So even if Lunar bonuses from shapeshifting count as dice from charms (which I assume they will), it's not enough to balance them on its own -- there will need to be other considerations across the Lunar charmset to balance out the fact that a Lunar shapeshifted into a bear is throwing around massive dice-pools for free that other people would have to burn motes every action to sustain. The trick is to do this in a way so that:<br /> <br /> 1. Shapeshifting is still awesome and makes you very very good at everything it should logically make you very very good at, and,<br /> 2. Shapeshifting isn't so essential that Lunars completely suck in human form.<br /> <br /> (Lunars have grappled with some variation of this problem in all editions, really, but it's a particularly thorny issue in 3e because nobody else really gets powerful scenelong buffs on par with turning into a bear. In some ways this is a good thing, mind, but it's still tricky to balance.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 11-01-2015, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T19:59:59-08:00","id":748259,"title":"","content":"I have wondered, considering John Morke said, IIRC, that in this edition Lunars would use the same charm XP costs as Solars, and that animal forms are more powerful, if it will no longer be free. If for example, Lunars will pay a small amount of XP (or a medium amount) to gain each form.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T20:32:08-08:00","id":748300,"title":"","content":"A bear is throwing around, best combat action, 12 dice in an attack. There are going to be a lot of Exalts that can statically keep up with that for 0 motes an action.<br /> <br /> The scene-long dice adding for being a bear seem pretty concentrated in the damage and soak areas, which have analogues in weapons and armor.<br /> <br /> Reflexive grapples and Berserker are pretty awesome, don't get me wrong, but I'm not seeing as much static dice adder problems as you describe. Am I missing something?<br /> <br /> Also, I've got a draft of Stamina up. So all of Lunars 2e Core is converted and now I'm moving on to the other books.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T00:07:38-08:00","id":748598,"title":"","content":"That's a fair point about equipment, at least for armour. Weapons not so much, since a bear's claws are going to be a light weapon anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T07:50:45-08:00","id":758651,"title":"","content":"I've edited and updated the three Charms posts. A few more 2e Lunar Core additions, some additional homebrew and some sprinkling of Dreams of the First Age Charms. See if I picked any of the broken ones!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}